{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_16093",
  "verbalization": "Olaparib, a poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor, is linked to Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary through a chain of indications involving Altretamine and Melphalan. The evidence suggests that Olaparib may be repurposed for this tumor type, as it is indicated for similar conditions like Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Immature Ovarian Teratoma, both of which are associated with Altretamine and Melphalan, respectively. The shared use of Altretamine in these contexts implies a potential mechanism of action or therapeutic relationship between Olaparib and these tumors. The indirect pathway through Melphalan further supports a possible role of Olaparib in treating this tumor type, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible repurposing of Olaparib for Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary, based on the overlapping indications and the shared use of related drugs.",
